No good!

74
00:05:55,740 --> 00:05:57,420
All right, you crazy kid!

75
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:58,360
Have at him!

76
00:05:58,900 --> 00:05:59,460
More!

77
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:00,920
He's fast!

78
00:06:03,140 --> 00:06:04,020
Come on!

79
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:05,100
Let's fight some more!

80
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:11,240
What the?

81
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:12,500
They won with one hit!

82
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:13,680
Crystal destroyed!

83
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:15,100
Team K wins!

84
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:16,660
Way to go!

85
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:18,660
Yeah, they really showed him, huh?

86
00:06:23,660 --> 00:06:24,380
Woohoo!

87
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:26,000
That was such a blast!

88
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,860
Oh, look, I can't believe I underestimated you!

89
00:06:28,940 --> 00:06:29,860
That was astounding!

90
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:31,560
Ding, ding, ladies and gents!

91
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,280
We have a winner!

92
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,080
So, Team K!

93
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:35,600
I'm so proud!

94
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:36,660
You did it, look!

95
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:38,660
That sneaky little rascal!

96
00:06:39,020 --> 00:06:39,500
Damn it!

97
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:41,300
I think he's too strong!

98
00:06:41,380 --> 00:06:42,820
Ha ha ha ha ha ha!

99
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:44,480
Ah ha ha ha!

100
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:46,980
Next, I'll be fighting him!

101
00:06:47,700 --> 00:06:48,900
Bet that'll be interesting!

102
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:51,060
I'll paint an even prettier picture!

103
00:06:52,060 --> 00:06:54,840
Now for the eighth and final match of the first round!

104
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:56,360
Teams O and P!

105
00:06:56,780 --> 00:06:57,260
Approach!

106
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:58,440
The last one!

107
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:00,120
And it's a real doozy, too!

108
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:01,000
I can't wait!

109
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:03,780
It's gonna be Yuno and Noel on a team together!

110
00:07:04,780 --> 00:07:06,280
Sheesh, that took long enough!

111
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:09,080
When all this is over with, you owe me a date!

112
00:07:09,420 --> 00:07:10,600
I don't think so.

113
00:07:10,840 --> 00:07:11,700
Who's their third?

114
00:07:13,020 --> 00:07:14,000
Hey, gang!

115
00:07:14,260 --> 00:07:15,000
Are you ready?

116
00:07:15,380 --> 00:07:18,320
If we all do our best, we're sure to make it through this round!

117
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:19,760
Can you make it through this day?

118
00:07:19,760 --> 00:07:22,800
I just know we're gonna succeed.

119
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:25,660
Do you think this guy is okay to participate?

120
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:27,480
Well...

121
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:30,820
Actually, now that I think about it, didn't you and Osta grow up together?

122
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:33,980
You'd better not act like an idiot out there like he would.

123
00:07:34,220 --> 00:07:35,360
Same goes for you.

124
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:38,160
I know magic control isn't your strong suit.

125
00:07:38,820 --> 00:07:41,900
You had your hands full using monoskin back at the volcano.

126
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,160
Are you up for this?

127
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:45,680
Excuse me?

128
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:47,800
Don't you realize you're in the presence of royalty?

129
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:51,540
I mean, let's be honest, you were raised to be a barbarian just like Osta was.

130
00:07:51,780 --> 00:07:54,440
Maybe you're too stupid to participate in this test!

131
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:55,820
Keep it down, princess!

132
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:59,360
Not only is that a weak argument, but how you phrased it was childish.

133
00:07:59,700 --> 00:08:02,340
It kind of makes me wonder if Osta's been rubbing off on you.

134
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:03,400
How dare you!

135
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:07,020
If you're saying I would let myself be influenced by a mediocre musclehead like Osta,

136
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:09,280
then you're just as much of an ignorant jerk as he is!

137
00:08:09,320 --> 00:08:11,600
And stop looking at me with that contestant face!

138
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:13,840
I'm the only one who's allowed to do that to people!

139
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:15,080
Do you understand me?

140
00:08:15,220 --> 00:08:15,740
Now, now.

141
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:18,060
You guys aren't being very good sports here.

142
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:20,100
Don't you think you ought to try to play nice?

143
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:22,900
I'm pretty sure you're the reason they're arguing, Osta.

144
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:23,660
Yeah, right!

145
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:25,600
Who would bother getting angry over you?

146
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:28,440
Now, I may have to get along with you for this match,

147
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:30,280
but that doesn't mean I have to like you!

148
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:31,600
I'm sorry!

149
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:33,020
Did I say you could touch me?

150
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:36,520
You must be confident if you've got time for chit-chat.

151
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:41,640
I'm shocked to find that the shame of how Silva is competing in this tournament.

152
00:08:42,180 --> 00:08:45,540
The Black Bulls may have recently ascended to just above absolute failure,

153
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:48,500
but you don't consider yourself responsible for that, right?

154
00:08:48,680 --> 00:08:50,260
Can we please not do this?

155
00:08:50,540 --> 00:08:53,580
I'm not surprised you haven't learned to control your magic power.

156
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:57,100
After all, you couldn't even get accepted into the Silver Eagles,

157
00:08:57,100 --> 00:08:59,960
despite the fact that you were a member of the Silva family.

158
00:09:00,860 --> 00:09:03,460
The jerk with the goofy haircut again, seriously?

159
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:08,440
What a waste of space.

160
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:11,560
If you're royalty, then how come you can't do all the amazing things

161
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:13,560
the rest of our family can, you little freak?

162
00:09:15,660 --> 00:09:16,280
That's odd.

163
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,940
I thought I trained you better than to start eating before I do.

164
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:26,140
Please give me my time back before you mess it up.

165
00:09:26,140 --> 00:09:27,360
I don't like this game.

166
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:28,880
If you weren't such a weakling,

167
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:32,120
then maybe you'd have the ability to protect all the things that are important to you.

168
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:34,120
Just give it back, okay?

169
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:43,860
If it makes you angry, then do something about it.

170
00:09:43,860 --> 00:09:47,360
Oh, wait, your dumb spells probably can't hit me, can they?

171
00:09:53,180 --> 00:09:54,020
Oh, great!

172
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:56,140
That demon raccoon is after you do again!

173
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:58,180
I was so dead, Parkourine!

174
00:09:58,420 --> 00:10:00,140
My eyeballs are killing me!

175
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:01,760
It's okay, you can do it, Noel.

176
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:04,920
Look at how much you've accomplished since you started your journey with the blood balls.

177
00:10:05,160 --> 00:10:05,860
We're cheering for you.

178
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:10,260
We know what you're capable of better than your brother to his friends and the family you choose.

179
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:15,320
So, if you can't believe in yourself, then just believe in the friends who believe in you.

180
00:10:15,540 --> 00:10:18,180
Does anybody know what he's mumbling about over there?

181
00:10:18,180 --> 00:10:22,140
I'd say he's putting some kind of unspeakable curse on that Silver Eagles guy.

182
00:10:22,140 --> 00:10:23,800
I think you've wasted enough time.

183
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:24,920
It's our turn to fight.

184
00:10:25,060 --> 00:10:26,580
Oh, well, I beg your pardon.

185
00:10:27,280 --> 00:10:28,560
I hope you're ready, Noel.

186
00:10:29,060 --> 00:10:29,780
Watch out.

187
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:30,680
Don't die.

188
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:31,680
Don't die.

189
00:10:31,680 --> 00:10:35,340
Don't die away, but it's over for you, bud!

190
00:10:49,340 --> 00:10:51,760
And now, the eighth match of round one!

191
00:10:52,140 --> 00:10:57,980
Team O, Alec Dora, Solid, and Dimitri, versus Team P, N, Yuno, and Noel.

192
00:10:58,480 --> 00:10:59,080
Let's begin!

193
00:10:59,520 --> 00:11:02,720
With Noel and Yuno on the same team, I know who's gonna win!

194
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:04,020
Let you in out!

195
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:05,140
We're rooting for you!

196
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:08,100
Show these boys the beautiful babes of the Black Bulls' main business!

197
00:11:08,700 --> 00:11:12,000
Remember not to go easy on him just because he's your big brother!

198
00:11:12,180 --> 00:11:13,720
All the more reason to beat him!

199
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:14,820
I'll do the attacking.

200
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:16,600
You two can back me up.

201
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:18,120
No, that should be my job.

202
00:11:18,220 --> 00:11:18,840
It's fine.

203
00:11:19,100 --> 00:11:20,020
Let me do it!

204
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:20,680
No, thanks.

205
00:11:21,020 --> 00:11:21,860
Listen here!

206
00:11:21,860 --> 00:11:24,680
I'll be happy on the defensive, actually.

207
00:11:25,540 --> 00:11:27,740
They're a lot faster than I thought.

208
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:29,200
What's happening?

209
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:39,360
Vexing as it is to do, this abridged version of that compound magic is a handy shortcut.

210
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:42,520
A single swift attack, and it's all over!

211
00:11:43,660 --> 00:11:46,280
Their team's crystal is still in its starting location.

212
00:11:47,020 --> 00:11:47,320
Damn.

213
00:11:47,720 --> 00:11:50,080
They're about to shatter ours in one fell swoop.

214
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:52,360
Wind magic.

215
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:52,720
Crescent Bye-bye.

216
00:11:52,780 --> 00:11:54,120
Crescent Moonshicle.

217
00:11:54,460 --> 00:11:54,820
Jesus.

218
00:11:55,540 --> 00:11:56,180
Flame magic.

219
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:57,560
Cambo eruption.

220
00:11:58,240 --> 00:11:59,380
Water magic.

221
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:00,060
See, dragon?

222
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:00,840
Fire!

223
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:07,480
So, the little neophyte thinks she can learn defensive spells, does she?

224
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:10,880
Sand magic suppressing sand mass!

225
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:16,680
It's absorbing all the water.

226
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:22,700
If this keeps up, we'll be stuck on the defensive.

227
00:12:23,780 --> 00:12:28,240
Listen, girl, this is not an opportunity to cozy up my Yuno, okay?

228
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:31,580
Here's the plan. I'm probably the fastest on the team.

229
00:12:32,260 --> 00:12:35,100
So I'm going to try to catch them off guard and destroy their crystal.

230
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:38,440
You and that other guy should focus on protecting arms.

231
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,680
Wait. Let me do this.

232
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:44,420
Please.

233
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:50,100
I'll stop you right here!

234
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:57,040
That's the stuff, Noelle!

235
00:12:58,240 --> 00:12:59,880
She's fought alongside Asta.

236
00:13:01,560 --> 00:13:02,580
She'll be fine.

237
00:13:05,380 --> 00:13:08,660
Besides, the crystal's safer with me guarding it.

238
00:13:09,240 --> 00:13:10,500
If it's me who goes.

239
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:12,920
I've got you now, Noelle.

240
00:13:13,580 --> 00:13:15,500
Solid's sure to be right on my heels.

241
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:19,340
I said to behave like you're part of the team!

242
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:25,920
Deal with him later. Fight me.

243
00:13:25,920 --> 00:13:30,100
Hey, did you hear about that four-leaf rookie?

244
00:13:31,700 --> 00:13:35,020
He took down one of the Diamond Kingdom's eight shining generals.

245
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:36,600
In his first year?

246
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:38,380
Now that's what I call impressive.

247
00:13:39,380 --> 00:13:40,860
Oh, and it gets better.

248
00:13:41,380 --> 00:13:46,200
After that, he took a shot at the vice-captain and said he'd be the captain of the Golden Dawn.

249
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:50,520
Just goes to show you, being chosen by the Wind Spear really sets you apart, doesn't it?

250
00:13:51,560 --> 00:13:54,020
Seems like Captain Vongens has high hopes for him.

251
00:13:55,580 --> 00:13:59,840
So you think you can eliminate me and protect your team's crystal at the same time?

252
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:03,440
There's that arrogance you're so famous for!

253
00:14:06,560 --> 00:14:08,500
Just fight like you mean it, okay?

254
00:14:09,700 --> 00:14:11,160
Why'd it have to be you?

255
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:20,120
I should have been ready for an ambush.

256
00:14:21,340 --> 00:14:25,120
I managed to escape, but I wound up in this deep cave.

257
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:28,060
Not much chance of someone coming to save me.

258
00:14:30,560 --> 00:14:31,800
So this is it.

259
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:39,140
There's no need to fear. I'll help you.

260
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:44,020
In that moment, he reminded me of a painting from my childhood.

261
00:14:44,660 --> 00:14:47,820
Of a kind and gentle god bathed in a soft light.

262
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:53,760
I sensed that you were in here.

263
00:14:54,580 --> 00:14:55,860
Your worries are over now.

264
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:04,220
Besides his magic, Captain Vongens has another strange power.

265
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:10,020
It's some kind of warmth that connects him to all of us squad members.

266
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:15,540
After that happened, I swore that I'd dedicate my grimoire to him.

267
00:15:15,540 --> 00:15:21,640
I strove to help the Golden Dawn remain the greatest of all the Magic Knight squads.

268
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:28,840
Because we are the noble elite, hand-selected by Sir Vongens himself.

269
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:32,840
So why was he made one of us?

270
00:15:33,460 --> 00:15:35,040
This backwoods commoner?

271
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:37,840
And what's more...

272
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:44,680
Even though he bonded with each of us impartially, it's plain to see that the Captain favors him the most.

273
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:47,640
But why? I don't understand.

274
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:49,200
You know.

275
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:54,320
Why has he said that lowlife's name five times today?

276
00:15:55,540 --> 00:15:58,120
And he hasn't spoken the first word to me!

277
00:15:59,420 --> 00:16:01,080
What makes him special?

278
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:02,880
The four-leaf clover?

279
00:16:03,640 --> 00:16:06,880
It's bad enough that he's regarded so highly above the rest of us.

280
00:16:07,380 --> 00:16:11,000
But for that urchin to declare that he'll become the next Captain of the Golden Dawn?

281
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:13,800
It's an insult to Sir Vongens!

282
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:18,480
Don't go getting a big head because you are lucky enough to end up with spirit magic!

283
00:16:18,480 --> 00:16:21,480
It was his amazing power that got him chosen in the first place!

284
00:16:21,580 --> 00:16:22,420
Thank you very much!

285
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:24,760
Boy, this guy ticks me off! Let's pummel him!

286
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:26,160
That's enough, Belle.

287
00:16:26,980 --> 00:16:30,700
Seriously? Don't tell me you're thinking about fighting him without letting me help!

288
00:16:37,660 --> 00:16:41,400
Leave it to useless Noel to try to win with one lousy defensive spell!

289
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:42,660
What's wrong with you?

290
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:46,860
We were supposed to hit their crystal at the same time, but you just ruined our strategy!

291
00:16:46,860 --> 00:16:50,600
Ah, quiet! What makes you think you get to tell me what to do?

292
00:16:50,940 --> 00:16:54,080
Okay, then. It looks like my only option is to back him up!

293
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:54,860
Hey!

294
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:55,700
Huh?

295
00:16:56,340 --> 00:16:59,020
What is that thing?

296
00:16:59,020 --> 00:17:07,820
Fungus magic running Mr. Mushroom.

297
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:11,000
I sprinkled a few spores on you when you weren't looking.

298
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:13,600
I'm not letting you stand in Noel's way.

299
00:17:17,320 --> 00:17:19,560
Honestly, I almost feel bad for you.

300
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:21,860
Any direction you go, I'll be right there.

301
00:17:21,860 --> 00:17:25,280
You don't stand a chance of putting so much as a scratch on my crystal.

302
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:28,480
Are you sure about that?

303
00:17:28,480 --> 00:17:29,980
Whoa! What's happening here?

304
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:31,920
Not to worry. It's me, N.

305
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:35,320
I'm talking to you via my voice transmitting talking mushroom.

306
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:38,360
You can't go around sticking creepy fungi on people!

307
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:41,200
I'll make it brief, but please hear me out.

308
00:17:41,700 --> 00:17:44,980
I've been listening to Solid since before the battle began.

309
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:48,640
The way that monster treats his baby sister is unacceptable.

310
00:17:49,540 --> 00:17:52,340
As the oldest of 11 children, it makes me sick.

311
00:17:52,700 --> 00:17:55,440
In fact, my siblings are the reason I'm fighting today.

312
00:17:56,720 --> 00:18:02,060
Noel, an older brother's most important job is to look after his siblings who are younger and weaker.

313
00:18:02,060 --> 00:18:08,180
But judging by the many hurtful things I've heard him say, it doesn't sound like he's even trying to uphold that responsibility.

314
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:10,000
So thrash him once and for all!

315
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:14,580
And I'm not talking about a slap on the wrist! I want you to pulverize this disgrace of a brother!

316
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:17,940
You've really perked up since the fight started, haven't you?

317
00:18:18,440 --> 00:18:23,300
Humans are like animals! If you put them firmly in their place, they'll never oppose you again!

318
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:25,540
Oh, this is absolutely hilarious!

319
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:30,080
Someone's getting thrashed, but it surely won't be me! Sorry!

320
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:34,420
I can crush you pathetic weaklings without drinking a sweat!

321
00:18:37,020 --> 00:18:39,640
That's right. I was weak before.

322
00:18:40,540 --> 00:18:45,820
And you, Solid. My entire life, you've always been my bigger, stronger, older brother.

323
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:50,100
But I'm done caring whether or not you approve of me.

324
00:18:52,340 --> 00:18:56,160
I've already earned the approval of people whose opinions matter a lot more than yours!

325
00:18:56,160 --> 00:19:01,480
Once upon a time, I was terrified of what your magic power could do.

326
00:19:01,980 --> 00:19:03,580
But now that just feels silly.

327
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:06,920
Who cares? You're still a failure!

328
00:19:07,760 --> 00:19:08,940
Water creation magic!

329
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:10,820
Slashing sea serpent!

330
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:14,580
Your existence is a slap in my face!

331
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:16,900
Sand creation magic!

332
00:19:17,420 --> 00:19:18,160
Sand armor!

333
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:19,680
Dreadnought guard!

334
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:22,140
This is my most powerful spell!

335
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:24,100
Offense and defense in one!

336
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:26,800
Try to stop that without spirit magic!

337
00:19:27,940 --> 00:19:31,460
I will be the one to bring Sarbange's extreme into reality!

338
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:34,640
Wind magic.

339
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:36,980
Towering tornado!

340
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:42,840
From the inside?

341
00:19:42,840 --> 00:19:48,160
Am I crazy or did Yuno somehow activate a spell inside his opponent's magic?

342
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:51,440
Skills like that and the ladies can't get enough of them?

343
00:19:51,580 --> 00:19:53,720
Damn, this guy really does have it going on!

344
00:19:56,020 --> 00:20:01,540
But that's his dream.

345
00:20:01,940 --> 00:20:03,100
It's not mine.

346
00:20:05,580 --> 00:20:08,760
I only fight for my own dream.

347
00:20:08,760 --> 00:20:13,820
That's absurd!

348
00:20:14,220 --> 00:20:14,740
Insane!

349
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:15,620
Preposterous!

350
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:17,180
It's downright impossible!

351
00:20:18,320 --> 00:20:20,000
What even is that magic?

352
00:20:22,500 --> 00:20:25,200
Noelle isn't capable of anything that powerful!

353
00:20:27,260 --> 00:20:27,980
Hey, Solid!

354
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:31,760
You might...

355
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:33,380
want a block.

356
00:20:34,380 --> 00:20:36,560
Just try to hit me, you pipsqueak!

357
00:20:36,560 --> 00:20:41,400
She looks strong, but there's no way one of her abilities could ever hurt me!

358
00:20:42,220 --> 00:20:43,100
Do your worst!

359
00:20:43,460 --> 00:20:44,960
You good-for-nothing girl!

360
00:20:45,420 --> 00:20:46,880
Sea Dragon's war!

361
00:20:55,460 --> 00:20:56,060
Awesome!

362
00:20:58,440 --> 00:20:59,140
She won!

363
00:20:59,520 --> 00:21:01,760
She wiped out their crystal in one hit?

364
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:03,360
Crystal destroyed!

365
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:04,860
Team P wins!

366
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:11,020
I'm not weak!

367
00:21:12,100 --> 00:21:12,660
Not anymore!

